# CODEOWNERS — GitHub uses this to auto-assign reviewers on PRs
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Format: <pattern>  <@github-username or @org/team>
# Replace placeholders below with your actual GitHub usernames.

# ── Default: all files require review from the lead dev ──────────────────────
*                           @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME

# ── Workflow & CI files — extra scrutiny ─────────────────────────────────────
.github/                    @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME

# ── Supabase / database migrations ───────────────────────────────────────────
supabase/                   @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME

# ── Environment & config files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.env*                       @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME
*.config.*                  @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME
vite.config.*               @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME
tsconfig*.json              @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME

# ── Source code — shared ownership across team ───────────────────────────────
src/                        @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME @TEAM-MEMBER-2

# ── Public assets — lighter touch ────────────────────────────────────────────
public/                     @YOUR-LEAD-DEV-USERNAME
